        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "bdJSz",
          "name": "Decoration Rules",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "fill": "$brand-mist",
          "cornerRadius": 12,
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 8,
          "padding": 22,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "iuPX6",
              "name": "Title",
              "fill": "$ink",
              "content": "Background decoration",
              "fontFamily": "$font-head",
              "fontSize": 16,
              "fontWeight": "700"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "n4nnGC",
              "name": "Desc",
              "fill": "$ink-muted",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Two motifs only: concentric spotlight rings and a fading dot grid — both pure vector (SVG in code, no image files, no extra weight). They appear ONLY in flat bands that would otherwise be empty: page heroes, the countdown strip, the registration hero, the CTA and newsletter bands, and the footer. Never behind photography, never behind body copy or forms. Each host section needs overflow:hidden so the motif bleeds off the edge. Opacity sits between 0.5 and 1 with stroke alpha around 25–30%, so the motif must stay invisible in a squint test — if you notice it before the headline, it is too strong. Decorative only: mark it aria-hidden.",
              "lineHeight": 1.65,
              "fontFamily": "$font-body",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "qp719",
          "name": "Rounded Band Pattern",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "fill": "$brand-mist",
          "cornerRadius": 12,
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 8,
          "padding": 22,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "cxad0",
              "name": "Title",
              "fill": "$ink",
              "content": "Rounded band pattern",
              "fontFamily": "$font-head",
              "fontSize": 16,
              "fontWeight": "700"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "Djq7C",
              "name": "Desc",
              "fill": "$ink-muted",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Coloured bands carry one large asymmetric corner so each block reads as a card sliding over the next one. Direction alternates down the page: heroes cut bottom-right, the CTA band cuts top-left. Desktop radius 100–140px, mobile 48–56px, all other corners square. Build it as two elements: an outer wrapper whose background is the colour of the ADJACENT section the corner exposes, and an inner band with border-radius plus overflow:hidden. Never let the page's white show through the cut — that is the whole point of the wrapper. Wrapper colours are named in the layer tree, e.g. “Hero Wrapper (bg = countdown strip)”. Footers stay square.",
              "lineHeight": 1.65,
              "fontFamily": "$font-body",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
